--- HARMONIC LADDER of the frozen comb -------------------------------
  The mm comb's fundamental sits far below the band the gate acts in,
  so the fundamental alone cannot express a tenth-pixel blur.  A tick
  is a narrow bar, so its harmonics carry real power at KNOWN
  frequencies -- n*f0 for the same physical pitch.  Each harmonic is
  admitted separately by the same INERT gate (S/B >= 3 at gate 0).

